{"skill":{"slug":"ai-data-analysis","displayName":"AI Data Analysis"},"version":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1771571081607,"changelog":"Initial release","changelogSource":"user","license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":958,"sha256":"2cb3a7637a1cfa57fb6d0b34172203d96bf4bc8c02899c146c831ae372bf68bb","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"main.py","size":2967,"sha256":"34b646caecc16daba6ff0f66e9814c2dfc7c7e9630fda462470c5915889e63f0","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"package.json","size":577,"sha256":"6d14f52178480c6a863575639d761f333fa71ada1fe25517ab1bfe23b48bc764","contentType":"application/json"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":1926,"sha256":"b28302209efbe5f62fa08c2c1514d5650810c0c7f22b5f193ac9db3f2ce75d49","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789074632941,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"25f9c2c9965972e2eba8a5540892fd0c2d7f1af5ddab3e11a6e8eb5e68f641a0","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/25f9c2c9965972e2eba8a5540892fd0c2d7f1af5ddab3e11a6e8eb5e68f641a0","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: ai-data-analysis\nVersion: 1.0.0\n\nThe skill bundle is classified as suspicious due to critical vulnerabilities in `main.py`. The script directly uses `sys.argv` for `file_path` and `output_format` without sufficient sanitization. This allows for arbitrary file read (including potential Server-Side Request Forgery via URLs) when `file_path` is passed to `pd.read_csv()`, and arbitrary file write via path traversal when `output_format` is used to construct output filenames (e.g., `../../../../tmp/malicious.sh`). These vulnerabilities could lead to remote code execution if exploited by a malicious user or a prompt-injected agent.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779165622436},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":22,"severity":"MEDIUM","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":5,"checkedAt":1789074632941},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"This skill is a simple local CSV analysis and cleaning tool with some documentation overclaims but no evidence of hidden, destructive, credential-seeking, or network behavior.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Runtime behavior is proportionate to the purpose: it reads only the file path provided by the user and writes derived outputs under the skill's local output directory.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The package metadata points to main.py and defines simple analyze and clean script aliases; no install hooks, remote downloads, dependency declarations, or tool wrapping behavior were found.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"Instructions are ordinary usage examples for running analysis or cleaning actions; they do not attempt to override agent behavior, alter safety rules, or request unrelated access.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The skill creates output files for reports or cleaned data, but it does not install persistent services, scheduled tasks, memory rules, credential stores, or elevated-privilege mechanisms.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The implemented code reads a user-supplied CSV and writes analysis or cleaned-data outputs, which matches the general data-analysis purpose, though the documentation advertises broader Excel, chart, PDF/HTML, anomaly, and trend features that are not implemented.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"note"}],"guidance":"Before installing, treat this as a basic CSV-only local analysis utility, not the full-featured Excel/chart/PDF service described in the README. Run it only on data you intend to analyze, and note that it writes report or cleaned-data files into its local output directory.","findings":"[SQP-3] unexpected: The Chinese documentation and mixed-language metadata are a localization/documentation concern, not evidence of hidden capability or unsafe behavior.\n[SQP-2] expected: Creating local reports and cleaned-data files is expected for a data-analysis tool; the documentation could better warn users that output files/directories will be created.\n[SDI-4] unexpected: The unused analysis_type parameter supports a capability-overclaim concern, but it only results in the same summary report being generated rather than unsafe behavior.\n[SQP-3] unexpected: Chinese docstrings in main.py are not user-impacting security behavior and do not create privilege, persistence, or data-access risk.\n[SQP-3] unexpected: The bilingual package description is a quality/localization issue rather than a security concern.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789074632941}}}}}